    "title": "Birth of Texas: An \"Act of Nature\" and the \"Blue Nun\" | Newsletters | itemonline.com",
    "text": "Our story begins in February of 1685, when René Robert Cavelier Sieur de La Salle, thinking he was near the mouth of the Mississippi River, sailed into Matagorda Bay far west of his intended target.\nBazaar circumstances left him with none of his initial four ships; there, his expedition lay stranded. Why would a seasoned explorer make such a glaring mistake in directions when just three years earlier he had led an expedition from Canada to the mouth of the Mississippi River?",
